## Step 5: Create Security Group
A Security Group acts as a **firewall** for your EC2 instances.--
### Navigate There:
```
EC2 → Security Groups (left sidebar) → Create Security Group
```--
### Fill in Basic Details:
```
Security group name:  secure-share-sg
Description:          
VPC:                  
```--
Security group for secure file sharing
secure-share-vpc   ← IMPORTANT: select your VPC, not default
### Inbound Rules — Add 2 rules:
Click **Add Rule** twice and fill in:
| # | Type | Protocol | Port Range | Source | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | SSH | TCP | 22 | **My IP** | Your laptop → EC2 |
| 2 | Custom TCP | TCP | 22 | `10.0.0.0/16` | VM-A ↔ VM-B internal |
> For Rule 1 → select **"My IP"** from the source dropdown — AWS auto-fills your 
current IP
> For Rule 2 → type `10.0.0.0/16` manually — this allows both VMs to talk to each 
other inside the VPC--
### Outbound Rules:
```
Leave as default → All traffic, 0.0.0.0/0    
```--
### Then click **Create Security Group**--
### It Should Look Like This:
```
