## Phase 5: Set Up SSH Keys (VM-A → VM-B)
This allows VM-A to securely transfer files to VM-B **without a password**--
### STEP 1: Generate SSH Key — Run on VM-A ONLY
```bash
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "vm-a-to-vm-b" -f ~/.ssh/vm_transfer_key
```
When prompted:
```
Enter passphrase: (just press Enter)        
← no passphrase
Enter same passphrase again: (Enter again)  ← no passphrase
```
Success looks like:
```
Your identification has been saved in /home/ubuntu/.ssh/vm_transfer_key
Your public key has been saved in /home/ubuntu/.ssh/vm_transfer_key.pub
The key fingerprint is:
SHA256:xxxxxxxxxxxxxx vm-a-to-vm-b    
```--
✅
### STEP 2: View & Copy Public Key — Run on VM-A ONLY
```bash
cat ~/.ssh/vm_transfer_key.pub
```
Output looks like:
```
ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA...........
............................................
vm-a-to-vm-b
```
>  
⚠
**Select ALL of this output and copy it**
> It starts with `ssh-ed25519` and ends with `vm-a-to-vm-b`--
### STEP 3: Add Key to VM-B — Run on VM-B ONLY
```bash
# Create .ssh directory
mkdir -p ~/.ssh
chmod 700 ~/.ssh
# Paste VM-A's public key here
echo "PASTE-VM-A-PUBLIC-KEY-HERE" >> ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
```
Example (yours will be different):
```bash
echo "ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA...vm-a-to-vm-b" >> 
~/.ssh/authorized_keys
```--
### STEP 4: Verify Key Added — Run on VM-B ONLY
cat ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
```
Should show your key:
```
ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA...vm-a-to-vm-b  
```--
### STEP 5: Test Connection — Run on VM-A ONLY
# Use VM-B's PRIVATE IP here
✅
ssh -i ~/.ssh/vm_transfer_key ubuntu@<VM-B-PRIVATE-IP>
First time prompt:
```
Are you sure you want to continue connecting? → type: yes
```
Success:
```
Welcome to Ubuntu 22.04 LTS
ubuntu@ip-10-0-1-xx:~$   
Then type:
exit   
## Yes! Paste the Actual Key — But It's NOT the IP Address!--
###  
```
⚠
Common Confusion:
IP Address:  13.127.189.130        
← This is NOT the key
Public Key:  ssh-ed25519 AAAA...   ← This IS what you paste
```--
### Go to VM-A Tab and Run:
```bash
cat ~/.ssh/vm_transfer_key.pub
```
You'll see output like this:
```
ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIBx3jxq2Kh9LmP
wRtYuIoP3qWeRtYuIoP3qWeRtYuIoP vm-a-to-vm-b
```
>  
⚠--
**Select and copy that ENTIRE line** starting from `ssh-ed25519`
### Then Go to VM-B Tab and Run:
```bash
echo "ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIBx3jxq2Kh9LmP
wRtYuIoP3qWeRtYuIoP3qWeRtYuIoP vm-a-to-vm-b" >> ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
```
> Replace what's inside the quotes with **your actual key from VM-A**
--
